From e1b0abb1d064bc05121dede918acc9cf0b32ca77 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: yaegerbomb42 <yaeger.james42@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 12:02:17 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] feat(ui): error handling, toasts, empty states (t14r)

- ErrorBoundary wraps the app with a recoverable fallback (reload / try again)
- Toast system (pure lib/ui/toasts reducer + ToastsProvider) surfaces provider and
  network failures as dismissible, auto-expiring toasts; engine.runAgents emits
  onError for the call layer to surface
- InputBar gains a "starting" phase: inputs disabled and a spinner while a local
  run is starting (guarded so server-streamed runs keep the Stop control)
- Terminal (ComputerScreen) and telemetry panels show friendly empty states when
  there are no events
- Unit tests: 11 checks covering the toast reducer and describeFailure mapping

Co-Authored-By: Claude Code <noreply@anthropic.com>
